0..79 Comment "// The loop is not reflexivity, the HoTT book\'s Lemma 6.4.1. The paths from the"
80..154 Comment "// circle\'s point to itself are the words over the loop and its inverse, a"
155..232 Comment "// presented type whose two cancellations converge, so two words are one path"
233..311 Comment "// exactly when their normal forms agree. `loop` and the empty word are normal"
312..391 Comment "// and differ at their first letter: they are apart, and a path between them is"
392..468 Comment "// eliminated by a match of no arm. The book reaches the same fact through a"
469..540 Comment "// universe and univalence; here it is the apartness rule at the words."
542..575 Comment "// The empty type and the circle."
